# CapacitaFlow - database Schema Blueprint

This file outlines the database schema and models managed by Sequelize in the backend.

## Models Schema

### Category
- `id` (STRING, Primary Key): Category identifier (e.g. 'seg').
- `label` (STRING): Display name of the category (e.g. '⚡ Seguridad').

### Course
- `id` (STRING, Primary Key): Course identifier.
- `name` (STRING): Name of the course.
- `maxPerSlot` (INTEGER, Default: 15): Maximum capacity per slot for this course.
- `categoryId` (STRING, Foreign Key): References `Category(id)`.
- `niv_id` (INTEGER, Nullable): Level identifier.
- `plantaNombre` (STRING, Nullable): Plant name.

### ScheduleSlot
- `id` (STRING, Primary Key): Slot identifier (e.g. 's171746...').
- `date` (DATEONLY, Required): Scheduled date.
- `start` (STRING): Start time (e.g. '09:00').
- `end` (STRING): End time (e.g. '11:00').
- `max` (INTEGER, Default: 0): Maximum slots capacity.
- `adminEmail` (STRING, Nullable): Email of the admin who scheduled it.
- `modality` (STRING, Default: 'presencial'): Modality of the session ('online' or 'presencial').
- `courseId` (STRING, Foreign Key): References `Course(id)`.

### Enrollment
- `id` (INTEGER, Primary Key, Auto-Increment)
- `slotId` (STRING, Foreign Key): References `ScheduleSlot(id)`.
- `workerId` (STRING): ID of the worker.
- `workerName` (STRING): Name of the worker.
- `workerRut` (STRING): RUT of the worker.
- `workerCargo` (STRING): Job position of the worker.
- `contractor` (STRING): Contractor name.
- `evaluation` (ENUM('pending', 'passed', 'failed'), Default: 'pending'): Worker evaluation status.

### Request
- `id` (STRING, Primary Key): Request identifier.
- `status` (ENUM('pending', 'approved', 'rejected'), Default: 'pending'): Approval status.
- `createdAt` (DATE, Default: NOW)
- `slotId` (STRING): Target slot ID.
- `courseId` (STRING): Target course ID.
- `contractorId` (STRING): ID of the contractor.
- `contractorName` (STRING): Name of the contractor.
- `contractorEmail` (STRING, Nullable): Email address of the contractor.
- `workerIds` (JSON): List of worker IDs and metadata requesting enrollment.
- `data` (JSON): Flex fields.

### User
- `id` (STRING, Primary Key): User identifier.
- `username` (STRING): Login username.
- `password` (STRING): Login password.
- `role` (ENUM('SuperAdmin', 'Contratista'), Default: 'Contratista'): User role.
- `name` (STRING): Profile name.
- `email` (STRING, Nullable): User's email address.
- `cot_id` (STRING): Contractor ID (if applicable).
- `cot_razon_social` (STRING): Contractor business name.
- `contractorName` (STRING, Nullable): Legacy contractor name.
- `plantas` (JSON): List of plants assigned.

## Schema Sync Notes
- Schema modifications are safely synchronized at runtime. Any conflict between existing rows and new schema definitions is dynamically resolved by the system (in the seeder and on server startup) prior to altering the schema. Discrepancies in ENUM fields are corrected via custom database modify queries.
- The seeder (`back/database/seed.js`) only creates base system users from `back/database/initial.json`. No sample categories, courses, schedules, or enrollments are seeded. All domain data is created by real users through the application.
- Database port defaults to `3306` inside docker container networks, and resolves to `DB_PORT` for local host environments.
- Category CRUD endpoints are exposed via `/api/v1/categories`.
- Frontend data objects read in views are tracked in the console for runtime debugging and telemetry.
